# Host simulation: candidate counts of the exact thread bound and the first finishing pass (300 rows per cell, 256 threads)

Bounds: m1 = min over threads of the thread maximum (k <= 256), gm = min over 256 m group maxima with m = ceil(k / 256) (a priori valid), gmh = the same with m = ceil(k / 512) (valid only when C >= k, the column P(C<k) is its failure rate), topm = min over threads of the exact per-thread m-th largest. C = items at or above the bound. S = ceil(C / 256) candidate slots per thread. ovf = fraction of rows with C above the cap. Pivot statistics are for the m1 bound (k <= 256) or gm (k > 256) on the striped arrangement: n1 = items in the pivot bin after the first offset-digit pass over the candidates (mean / p90 / max), krem = remaining k inside the pivot bin (mean / max), done1 = fraction of rows with n1 == krem, le32 = fraction with n1 <= 32, dist = distinct keys in the pivot bin (mean), n2 = pivot bin after the second offset digit (mean / max), ew1 = the float equi-width pivot bin of N6 for comparison (mean / max).

